comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T14:23:58.574Z","harness:claude-code","Scope input 2026-07-31 from pm-aka8m7. This chore consolidates the load, verify, rewrite, re-anchor, report pipeline across redact, repair and compact, and that consolidation is the right and only place to add one thing all three paths currently omit.\n\nreanchorHistoryEntries at src/core/history/replay.ts:365-370 overwrites before_hash and after_hash in place and retains the prior values nowhere - the result carries an entriesRehashed count and a per-entry rehashed boolean. Every one of the three commands this chore unifies therefore destroys the anchors its inputs committed to, and so does every union merge, since src/sdk/merge/three-way.ts:57 documents reanchored as true for every union. Adding retention per command would mean writing it three times and would leave the merge driver's own path a fourth; adding it at the unified pipeline covers all four at once.\n\nRecommend widening this chore's acceptance criteria to include the retention hook - the shared pipeline emits the original anchor pair for each rewritten entry to whichever durable sink the owning command chooses - without taking on the storage-location decision, which belongs to pm-aka8m7. That keeps this chore mechanical while making the fix a one-site change afterwards rather than a four-site one."
body: ""
